<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60509" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύβηβος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύβη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stooping with the head,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				543.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύβηβος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ὁ</span>,
				<i>minister of Cybele</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				36
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυβέβις: γάλλος,
			κτλ</span>., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: generally, <i>one ecstatic</i> or <i>frantic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				82
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῠβηβάω</span></b> , <i>to be frantic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				543.11
			</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βειν</span> codd.):— <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> also has the forms <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυβήκη</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				120
			</span></i>) and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύβηκος</span></b> .</div>
